  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 has strong reporting deadlines and broad scope but no explicit during-investigation clause. S2 keeps a 5% permanent limit and customer disclosure, but allows a 36-month remediation with only a discretionary 8% earlier-pause trigger, likely weakening the interim cap. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 2 years (beyond acceptable 12 months) and retrofit at 6 years; S4 is a 36-month built-in suppression requirement; S5 has an 8/100k mandatory recall trigger with prompt customer notice and no serious-injury clause."
